{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the dogs are greedy.</b> Most occurrences of נפש in Scripture refer to the faculty that craves food, as in ונפשו מאכל תאוה (Job 33:20). The meaning: for all these dogs there is no benefit in them, only harm, for they are strong in desire, and this is greed of soul, and they are never sated. Behold the metaphor:" "<b>And they.</b> The meaning: the dogs mentioned — they are the shepherds of Israel who did not know understanding. שם הפועל." "<b>Each to his gain.</b> What does it profit him anything, as in מה בצע בדמי (Psalms 30:10)." "<b>[from his end].</b> Each one from his end."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 56, :notes {0 "The bracketed editorial note צ״ל כל corrects על to כל in the phrase כי על אלה; I have translated according to the correction."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:52.180948238Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}